# Canonical per-repo rally ledger.
#
# Append-only across all worktrees and branches. `merge=union` makes git
# concatenate both sides on merge instead of producing a conflict — which is
# the correct behavior for an append-only event log: the merged file is the
# union of all events anyone has ever recorded. Rally tolerates duplicate
# lines on replay (dedup by sequence_number), so this is safe.
#
# R5 supersedes the single `.rally/ledger.jsonl` monolith with per-engagement
# segments under `.rally/log/<engagement>.jsonl` (plus the migrated archive).
# The legacy line is preserved here for repos still mid-migration.
.rally/ledger.jsonl merge=union
.rally/log/*.jsonl merge=union
.rally/archive/*.jsonl merge=union
